    """Swap every staged member into its final name, one member at a time.

    The member rename is the only critical point: the live member goes
    aside to a detached name and the complete staging chain takes its
    place in two directory-entry changes under the parent and member
    locks, so the family member is always either the old complete chain
    or the new complete chain.  The detached old chain -- its shared
    slots hard-linked into the new one -- is emptied afterwards,
    releasing only the references the replacement drops.  A killed
    publish leaves both names recognizable; a re-run finishes it.
    """
    for member, path in zip(plan, target_paths):
        name = member["name"]
        final = os.path.join(parent, name)
        staging = _staging_path(parent, name)
        detached = _detached_path(parent, name)
